cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ThermalStorageBench, please cite the article and the dataset."
title: "ThermalStorageBench: A CFD benchmark for machine learning in sensible and latent thermal energy storage"
type: dataset
version: "1.0.0"
authors:
  - family-names: Bhattarai
    given-names: Saxam
    affiliation: Kathmandu University
  - family-names: Baral
    given-names: Bivek
    affiliation: Kathmandu University
  - family-names: Davidsson
    given-names: Henrik
    affiliation: Lund University
# license: CC-BY-4.0          # proposed for the data and checkpoints; code proposed MIT (decision pending)
# doi: 10.5281/zenodo.XXXXXXX # reserved DOI, to be added
# repository-code: https://github.com/<owner>/<repo>
keywords:
  - thermal energy storage
  - benchmark dataset
  - phase change material
  - stratified tank
  - neural operator
  - computational fluid dynamics
abstract: >-
  Transient two-dimensional OpenFOAM simulations for machine learning in thermal energy storage: 1,212
  charging and discharging runs of stratified water tanks and 500 melting runs of finned and tilted PCM
  cells (n-octadecane and lauric acid), with fixed design-level splits, engineering metrics, baselines,
  verification cases, validation against experiments, and 204 rescored network checkpoints.
